 "note": "The dock as three icons (AR12). One piece of a fixed size, bottom centre. Every place is in points from the body's top left; an image's `at` is its own top left, and it's shown at its `points` (or the `size` given, for the light, which stretches between its `cut` ends). A white image takes its tint; the body, the marks and the pip are in colour. A tile leans: its `box` is the box round it, the tap. It replaces the dock of buttons with words (hud_colour.json, pieces.dock, BlockDock).",
 "stack": [
  "DockBody at its `at`",
  "each button: open, its halo in its colour; at rest, its light's glow in its colour; then its light",
  "each button: its tile under its state's gradient, top to foot; at rest its sheen in its pale; open, its rim; its mark, its middle at `mark.middle`, `mark.size` across; its pip when it has something new"
 ],
 "states": {
  "rest": "the tile's gradient, the sheen, the light and its glow in the system's colour",
  "pressed": "the tile's pressed image at `tilePressed` (1.6 shorter, its foot where it was) under pressed's gradient, no sheen; the mark 1.6 lower and 0.32 to the left; the light in the system's deep, no glow",
  "open": "the tile white-hot under its gradient, its rim over it, its halo under it, the light white; the mark stays in ink",
  "new": "DockPip over the tile's far corner, in any state"
 },
